(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #130: a text the program only learns at run time is
 read as a number when the program runs. When it is not one, the error
 flag goes up and the sentence that stores it changes nothing: every
 spelling of a write keeps the old value, and a declaration holds its
 type's default. The flag is still up after the rest of the value has
 run, even past a division, which clears it on success.)

a text called word is "hello".
a number called count is 5.
Set count to word as a number.
On error print "Set kept {count}".
count is word as a number.
On error print "bare is kept {count}".
the count is {word as a number} add 1.
On error print "the is kept {count}".
Set count to {word as a number} divide 1.
On error print "after a division, kept {count}".
a number called fresh is word as a number.
On error print "a declaration holds {fresh}".
a float called ratio is 2.5.
Set ratio to word as a float.
On error print "a float kept {ratio}".

(A text is a number only when the whole of it could be written as a
 number literal in Vox source. None of these could: a word after the
 digits, nothing at all, a sign with no digits, a prefix with no digit of
 its base, two signs, a sign after the digits, a space on either side, a
 plus sign, an exponent, and a point with no digit on one side of it.)

a text called sample is "12 apples".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "1.5x".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "-".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "0x".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "0o8".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "0b2".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "--1".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "1-".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "7 ".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to " 7".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "+7".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "1e5".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to "3.".
Set count to sample as a number.
On error print "[{sample}] kept {count}".
Set sample to ".5".
Set ratio to sample as a float.
On error print "[{sample}] as a float kept {ratio}".
Set sample to "1e5".
Set ratio to sample as a float.
On error print "[{sample}] as a float kept {ratio}".
Set sample to "9223372036854775808".
Set ratio to sample as a float.
On error print "[{sample}] as a float kept {ratio}".

(A value read out of a list slot, and a value retyped in place, follow
 the same rule.)

a list called replies is [].
append "7 days" to replies.
append 5 to replies.
Set count to element 1 of replies.
On error print "a list slot kept {count}".
a value called answer is "7 days".
answer is a number.
On error print "a retyped value kept {answer}".

To tally with a text called reply.
  a number called total is 3.
  Set total to reply as a number.
  On error print "a local kept {total}".

tally with word.
